<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. The Board have recommended a dividend of Rs.1.20 per Equity share of Rs.2/­ each (60%) which is subject to approval of shareholders.  n2. The results  are  drawn  in  accordance  with  the  accounting  policies consistently followed by the company (also refer Note 2 below).  n3. IND AS 116  Leases  has been adopted effective 1-4-2019 and applied to all lease contracts existing on 1-4-2019 using modified retrospective approach. Effect of the adoption is not material to these financial results.  n4. As per  amendment  made by DOF vide notification dtd  30-3-2020 in Modified NPS - III Policy of Urea effective  from  2-4-2014 the co. will be compensated additional Rs.500 per MT for Urea sales from April,2014 onwards. Accordingly, the company has recognized Urea subsidy income of   Rs.103.75 Crores in Q4' 2019-20 out of which Rs.87.48 Crores pertains to previous years, Rs.11.60 Crores pertains to the 9 months from April 2019 to Dec. 2019 and Rs.4.68 Crores pertains to Q4' 2019-20.  n5. In assessing the recoverability  of receivables and certain investments, the company has considered internal  and external  information up  to  the  date  of  approval of  these financial statements  and economic  forecasts. Based on current indicators of future economic conditions, the company expects to recover the carrying amount of these assets. The impact of the global health pandemic may be different from that estimated as at the date of approval of these financial statements and the company will continue to closely monitor any material changes to future economic conditions.  n6. At present production at Polymer Unit has been stopped from Feb., 2020 due to economic unviability. Value in use of Polymer Unit is higher compared to its carrying value as on 31-3-2020.  n7. The Company is a large corporate as per the applicability criteria  given under the SEBI circular SEBI/HO/DDHS/CIR/P/2018/144 dated 26-11-2018 and has made disclosure as per the said circular.  n8. Relevant information required pursuant to SEBI circular dated 22-10-2019 and Regulation 52(4) of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015 in respect of listed Commercial Papers is as follows:  na)  The company has credit rating of  CARE A1+  and  IND A1+  on short term  by CARE Ratings Limited &amp; India Rating &amp; Research Pvt. Ltd respectively, for  its Commercial Papers at the time of issue. b)  The company has calculated following ratios:  nParticulars,31-03-2020  ni)  Debt Equity Ratio (in times)=0.23, ii) Debt Service Coverage Ratio (in times)=2.52, iii) Interest Service Coverage Ratio (in times)=3.74  nThe above ratios have been computed as under:  ni) Debt Equity Ratio (in times): (Long-Term  and Short-Term Borrowings including current maturity of Long-Term Borrowing)/Total Equity, ii) Debt  Service Coverage Ratio (in  times): (Profit  before  Depreciation, Finance Costs, Exceptional Items and Tax) /(Finance Cost + Principal Repayment of Long Term Borrowings), iii) Interest  Service Coverage Ratio (in times): (Profit  before  Depreciation, Finance Costs, Exceptional Items and Tax) /Finance Cost  nc)  The  Company  has  repaid  commercial  papers  on  their  respective  due  dates. The commercial papers of the company outstanding as on 31-3-2020 are Rs.300.00 Cr.  n9. The above financial results have been reviewed by the Finance-Cum-Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at their meetings held on 17th and 18th June, 2020 respectively.  n10. The figures of the current quarter and quarter ended 31-3-2019 are the balancing figures between audited figures for the full F.Y. and unaudited published year to date figures up to the 3rd qtr. ended 31-12-2019 and 31-12-2018, respectively.  n11. The Consolidated Financial Results for year ended 31-3-2020 and 31-3-2019 include results of Subsidiary- GATL, Subsidiary of subsidiary GASPL, Asso. companies- GGRC, VECL and Karnalyte Resources Inc.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
